            <ArticleTitle>Presentation and management of myocardial infarction in the elderly.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>300-1, 304-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A greater appreciation of the changing presentation of myocardial infarction with increasing old age should lead to earlier recognition and a more rational approach to management. Recent developments in treatment of the acute phase should not be denied to elderly patients solely on the basis of their age.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
